        "ADMIN",
        "POS",
        "SPA",
        "VISITOR"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Advise on revenue optimization and POS commerce with corporate authority.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 06 — POS MATRIX (Point of Sale — Restaurant, Spa, Retail).\n\nHOW IT WORKS:\n  1. Staff select a PRODUCT from the scrollable product grid (organized by category)\n  2. Use + / - to set quantity, then ADD TO CART\n  3. Cart shows all items with subtotal, VAT (15%), service charge (10%), and grand total\n  4. Choose payment method:\n     ROOM CHARGE: Posts to the guest's open folio (ONLY works if guest is IN-HOUSE — prevents revenue leakage)\n     CASH / CARD: Direct payment at terminal\n\nPRODUCT CATEGORIES: Food & Beverage, Spa Treatments, Shop items, Minibar.\nBarcode scanning is supported for shop/inventory items.\n\nAUTO-INTEGRATIONS (happens automatically on every sale):\n  → Inventory deducted: Ingredients/items deducted from Inventory Vault (Z-12) instantly\n  → Ledger posted: Double-entry posted to Accounts (Z-11) as CREDIT to F&B Revenue\n  → Folio updated: If room charge, guest's folio balance increases immediately\n\nPOS ADMIN (separate Z-POSADMIN): CDO-only panel to manage product prices, categories, add/remove items.\nTo set product prices, go to Inventory (Z-12) or POS Admin.\n\n[EXACT UI BUTTONS: ROOM CHARGE, ADD TO CART, +, -, VOID CART, NEXT, PREV, PUSHING..., PROCESSING...]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-25",
      "name": "Guest Marketing",
      "path": "/dashboard/guest-marketing",
      "icon": "📱",
      "sidebar_label": "GUEST MARKETING",
      "permissions": [
        "CDO",
        "GM",
        "ADMIN",
        "VISITOR"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Architect the digital bridge between our physical habitat and guest companions.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 25 — GUEST MARKETING ENGINE.\n\nPURPOSE: Digital marketing and guest app distribution hub.\n\nFEATURES:\n  APK DISTRIBUTION: The Miracle OS Guest App APK is available at https://miracle.vigilantitsolution.com/downloads/MiracleOS-GuestApp.apk.\n  WhatsApp Blast: Send the APK download link to any guest's WhatsApp in one tap.\n  PROMOTIONAL BROADCASTS: Create and send promotional offers to guest segments (VIP, all guests, specific dates).\n  LOYALTY COIN CAMPAIGNS: Issue bonus coins as promotional incentives.\n  ANALYTICS: View how many guests downloaded the app, engagement rates.\n\nGUEST APP FEATURES (what guests can do in the app):\n  Request room service, order food from the menu, view real-time folio balance,\n  redeem loyalty coins, communicate with front desk, check out.\n  All guest app requests flow directly to Command Grid (Z-07) and Solve Portal (Z-17).\n\n[EXACT UI BUTTONS: EXECUTE PUSH, CONSTRUCT NEW OFFER BROADCAST, PROMOS, DISTRIBUTION, ANALYTICS]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-08",
      "name": "Checkout/Billing",
      "path": "/dashboard/checkout",
      "icon": "💳",
      "sidebar_label": "CHECKOUT/BILLING",
      "permissions": [
        "CDO",
        "GM",
        "ADMIN",
        "FD",
        "POS",
        "SPA",
        "ACC",
        "VISITOR"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Control final settlements and folio closures with financial dominance.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 08 — FINANCIAL SETTLEMENT (Checkout & Billing).\n\nHOW TO CHECK OUT A GUEST:\n  1. Search for the guest by name or room number — their full folio loads\n  2. FOLIO DISPLAY: All itemised charges shown — room nights, F&B, spa, extras, advance deposit\n  3. BALANCE = Total charges - Advance deposit already paid\n  4. Select payment method(s): CASH, VISA, MASTERCARD, AMEX\n  5. Apply discount if authorised (hard rule: discount cannot exceed total bill)\n  6. Split-bill: Can split across multiple payment methods\n  7. Click CHECKOUT & SETTLE FOLIO\n\nWHAT HAPPENS ON CHECKOUT:\n  → Accounts (Z-11): Double-entry posted — credits Advance Deposit liability, debits Cash/Revenue\n  → Room status: Changes to DIRTY automatically, triggering housekeeping\n  → Folio: Locked as SETTLED, history preserved in CRM\n  → Guest loyalty coins: Calculated and added to guest CRM profile\n\nDEEP RE-SYNC: Force-pulls latest folio data from database if display seems stale.\nAWAITING TERMINAL SWIPE: Status indicator when card terminal is processing.\n\nRULE: Cannot checkout if outstanding balance > 0 without a payment method selected.\n\n[EXACT UI BUTTONS: DEEP RE-SYNC, AWAITING TERMINAL SWIPE..., VISA, MASTERCARD, AMEX, CASH, CHECKOUT & SETTLE FOLIO]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-16",
      "name": "Issue Tickets",
      "path": "/dashboard/issue-tickets",
      "icon": "📢",
      "sidebar_label": "ISSUE TICKETS",
      "permissions": [
        "ANY"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Dispatch service missions and maintenance tickets with operational authority.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 16 — ISSUE TICKETS (Fault Reporting Hub).\n\nPURPOSE: Any staff member can raise a complaint or fault ticket from any zone. This zone is the central view.\n\nHOW TO RAISE A TICKET:\n  Fill in: Room/Area, Department responsible, Subject/Description, Priority (LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/CRITICAL).\n  Assign to: Specific staff member or department.\n  Submit → Ticket created with unique ID, timestamp, status OPEN.\n\nTICKET STATES: OPEN → IN-PROGRESS → RESOLVED → CLOSED.\nRESOLVE FRACTURE on Command Grid (Z-07) room cards links directly to the ticket for that room.\n\nDATA SOURCE: solve_missions table. SQL: SELECT * FROM solve_missions WHERE status != 'CLOSED' ORDER BY priority DESC.\n\n[EXACT UI BUTTONS: RAISE TICKET, RESOLVE, ASSIGN, FILTER BY PRIORITY, FILTER BY DEPT]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-17",
      "name": "Solve (Staff)",
      "path": "/dashboard/solve",
      "icon": "🛠️",
      "sidebar_label": "SOLVE (STAFF)",
      "permissions": [
        "ANY"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Orchestrate the resolution of field missions to preserve habitat integrity.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 17 — SOLVE PORTAL (Staff Action Terminal).\n\nPURPOSE: Staff-facing task management. Shows all assigned tickets for the logged-in staff member.\nStaff can: view their assigned tasks, update status to IN-PROGRESS, mark as RESOLVED with notes.\nCDO view: Can see ALL tickets across all departments, override assignments, and close tickets.\nLinked directly to Issue Tickets (Z-16) — same data, different role-filtered view.\n\n[EXACT UI BUTTONS: MARK IN-PROGRESS, RESOLVE WITH NOTES, REASSIGN, VIEW ALL (CDO only)]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-20",
      "name": "Synapse Nexus",
      "path": "/dashboard/synapse",
      "icon": "⚡",
      "sidebar_label": "SYNAPSE NEXUS",
      "permissions": [
        "CDO",
        "GM",
        "ADMIN",
        "VISITOR",
        "SYNAPSE"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Supreme commander of the Synapse Nexus War Room. Orchestrate directives, communications, and strategic execution.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 20 — SOVEREIGN SYNAPSE NEXUS (Strategic Command, Communication & Execution Matrix).\n\nPURPOSE: The enterprise War Room. Combines HR org-chart, strategic task management, real-time P2P video conferencing, and the Corporate Matrix (Synapse Command Grid). Goes beyond Jira and Teams — it physically models the HR hierarchy and links strategic directives directly to field tickets and departmental neon signals.\n\nPANEL 1 — NEURAL TREE (Left): Live HR org-chart built from the Employee registry. CEO > Director > Manager > Operative hierarchy. ON-DUTY staff glow neon green. OFFLINE staff are dimmed. Click any node to open a radial action menu: VIDEO CALL, VOICE LINK, SEND SECURE FILE, ASSIGN DIRECTIVE.\n\nPANEL 2 — WAR ROOM KANBAN & COMMAND GRID (Center): Dual-view matrix. \n  VIEW A (KANBAN): Strategic Directives board with 4 columns: BACKLOG | ACTIVE | REVIEW | SECURED.\n  VIEW B (COMMAND GRID): Large Neon Glass Tiles for every Department (IT, HR, ACCOUNTS) and Corporate Area (POOL, SPA, BOARDROOM). Mimics the Z-07 Room Grid. When a directive node is assigned to a department, the corresponding tile pulses with a Cyan Neon glow and shows a badge (e.g., [3] pending). Multi-department tasks split into Nodes via the AGI Arbitrator, triggering multiple department pulses simultaneously.\n\nPANEL 3 — COMM-LINK (WebRTC): Click VIDEO CALL on any org-chart node to open the Conference Modal — a frosted glass overlay that slides in from the top. Multi-participant video grid. Controls: MUTE, CAM OFF, HANG UP. SOVEREIGN FREQUENCIES: Persistent voice channels (HK Frequency 1, Maintenance Channel, Management Room) — click to jack in.\n\nSECURE FILE EXCHANGE: Drop a PDF/file onto the War Room canvas. It routes to the selected operative's feed as a glowing Data Chip. Full audit trail logged.\n\nDATA SOURCES: /api/synapse/org-chart (HR tree), /api/synapse/directives (Kanban), /api/synapse/webrtc/create-room (conference), WS /ws/synapse/signal/{room_id} (P2P signaling).\n\n[EXACT UI BUTTONS: NEW DIRECTIVE, ASSIGN DIRECTIVE, SPAWN TO Z-16, VIDEO CALL, VOICE LINK, SEND SECURE FILE, HANG UP, MUTE, CAM OFF, JACK IN, RUN PAYROLL, TOGGLE COMMAND GRID]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-18",
      "name": "Biometric Portal",
      "path": "/dashboard/portal",
      "icon": "👁️",
      "sidebar_label": "BIOMETRIC PORTAL",
      "permissions": [
        "CDO",
        "GM",
        "ADMIN",
        "HR",
        "VISITOR"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Guard the boundaries of the ecosystem with biometric security precision.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 18 — BIOMETRIC SECURITY LAYER. Manages staff attendance via biometric sync. Shows login session history including: staff name, login time, logout time, zone accessed, and outcome (SUCCESS or FAILED). Failed login attempts are flagged. Prevents unauthorized access to restricted zones. Biometric shift data feeds directly into HR (Z-09) for payroll calculation — only verified biometric hours count toward salary. The session logs are immutable and feed into the Accounts audit trail (Z-11). [EXACT UI BUTTONS: MAPPING PORT..., VERIFY LOGIN]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-12",
      "name": "Inventory Matrix",
      "path": "/dashboard/inventory",
      "icon": "📦",
      "sidebar_label": "INVENTORY MATRIX",
      "permissions": [
        "CDO",
        "GM",
        "ADMIN",
        "POS",
        "HK",
        "MN",
        "VISITOR"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Custodian of the inventory vault and essential resort resources.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 12 — INVENTORY MATRIX (Stock Control Vault).\n\nPURPOSE: Tracks every physical item in the resort — F&B ingredients, spa supplies, minibar items, retail shop products.\n\nWHAT IT SHOWS:\n  Product grid with: Product ID, Name, Category, Department, Current Stock, Minimum Level (reorder point), Purchase Price (PP), Retail Price (RP).\n  LOW STOCK ALERT: Items below minimum level flash red — triggers a predictive reorder warning.\n  ASYNC SYNC INVENTORY: Forces immediate sync from all POS deductions (ensures stock count matches reality after a busy period).\n\nHOW STOCK MOVES:\n  Every POS sale auto-deducts matched ingredients from stock.\n  Manual stock-in: Add received goods manually with quantity and purchase price.\n  Variance: If physical count differs from system count, log discrepancy here.\n\nBOM (Bill of Materials): For F&B items, each menu item has a recipe — when a dish is sold, all ingredient quantities are deducted automatically.\n\nDATA SOURCE: inventory table. SQL: SELECT * FROM inventory WHERE stock < min_level for reorder report.\n\n[EXACT UI BUTTONS: ASYNC SYNC INVENTORY, ADD STOCK, EDIT ITEM, DELETE ITEM, LOW STOCK FILTER]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-09",
      "name": "HR / Personnel",
      "path": "/dashboard/hr",
      "icon": "👥",
      "sidebar_label": "HR / PERSONNEL",
      "permissions": [
        "CDO",
        "GM",
        "ADMIN",
        "HR",
        "VISITOR"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Curator of human capital, performance, and operational ROI.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 09 — HUMAN CAPITAL COMMAND (HR Panel). Full staff lifecycle management.\n\nTABS:\n  TAB: GALLERY — Visual biometric card grid of all staff operatives.\n    Each card shows: Photo/Avatar, Name, Job Title, Status (ON-DUTY/OFFLINE/TERMINATED), ROI score, Efficiency %.\n    Click any card → opens full DOSSIER OVERLAY with all financial and performance data.\n    From dossier: Generate Payslip, Generate Appointment Letter, Update avatar photo.\n\n  TAB: PERFORMANCE — Analytics table showing:\n    Operative name, Base Salary, Revenue Impact (what revenue they generated), Efficiency %, ROI Factor.\n    Data source: /api/hr/performance-matrix endpoint, pulling from employees table.\n\n  TAB: PAYROLL — Payroll execution table:\n    Shows each staff member's Monthly Hours, Total Payout (Base + Commission on revenue).\n    PUSH TO ACCOUNTS & INBOX button: Executes payroll for individual staff — posts to Accounts (Z-11) as DEBIT Payroll Expense and generates payslip document.\n    Total Payroll Liability shown in top-right chip.\n\n  TAB: DOCUMENTS — Document management:\n    DUBAI 5-STAR VAULT: Library of uploaded SOPs, Handbooks, Policies. Upload PDF/DOCX.\n    APPOINTMENT LETTER FORGE: Auto-generates appointment letters for any staff member in the MANTALA WORD MODULE editor.\n    MANTALA WORD MODULE: In-browser rich text editor — edit, save draft, print/export to PDF.\n\n  TAB: ONBOARDING — New staff registration:\n    Form fields: First Name, Last Name, Designation, Department (HK/MN/FD/POS/SPA/IT/AUDIT/SEC), Access Zone (RBAC checkboxes), Base Salary, Commission Rate %.\n    Upload PERSONAL AVATAR (UI display image) and BIOMETRIC SCAN (fingerprint/retina image).\n    On submit: Creates staff record in PostgreSQL, auto-generates username (FirstnameLastname format) and secure password, shows credentials banner.\n\n  TAB: REGISTRY — Surgery-level credential editor:\n    Editable table: Username, Password, Salary, Commission %, Status for every staff member.\n    Direct image upload from this table.\n    AUTHORIZE GLOBAL SYNC: Pushes ALL registry changes to PostgreSQL in one shot.\n\n  TAB: MY_SOP — Department SOP viewer pulled from Policy Engine (Z-19).\n\nDATA SOURCE: /api/hr/performance-matrix, /api/hr/onboard, /api/hr/sync-registry, /api/hr/execute-payroll/{id}\n\n[EXACT UI BUTTONS: GALLERY, PERFORMANCE, PAYROLL, DOCUMENTS, ONBOARDING, REGISTRY, MY_SOP, GENERATE DNA & AUTHORIZE ACCESS, PUSH TO ACCOUNTS & INBOX, AUTHORIZE GLOBAL SYNC, PRINT / PDF EXPORT, LOAD TO EDITOR, GENERATE IN EDITOR]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-10",
      "name": "CRM / Guest Loyalty",
      "path": "/dashboard/crm",
      "icon": "🤝",
      "sidebar_label": "CRM / GUEST LOYALTY",
      "permissions": [
        "CDO",
        "GM",
        "ADMIN",
        "FD",
        "VISITOR"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Architect of long-term guest bonds and the loyalty ecosystem.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 10 — CRM / GUEST LOYALTY ENGINE.\n\nPURPOSE: Full guest relationship management — tracks every guest who has ever stayed.\n\nWHAT IT SHOWS:\n  - Complete guest list with: Full Name, VIP Tier (Bronze/Silver/Gold/Platinum), Total LTV (Lifetime Value in revenue generated), Loyalty Coins balance, Phone, Email, Last Stay date.\n  - Search and filter by name, tier, or date range.\n  - VIP tier automatically upgrades based on total LTV thresholds.\n\nACTIONS PER GUEST:\n  - View full booking history (every stay, every spend)\n  - WhatsApp direct message button\n  - Issue loyalty coins manually\n  - View all folio charges across all stays\n\nLOYALTY COINS: Earned on every checkout (1 coin per currency unit spent). Can be redeemed for discounts on future stays via the Guest App.\n\nDATA SOURCE: guest_crm table, linked to guest_folios and reservations.\nSQL: SELECT * FROM guest_crm ORDER BY total_ltv DESC for top guests.\n\n[EXACT UI BUTTONS: SEARCH, VIEW HISTORY, SEND WHATSAPP, ISSUE COINS]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-11",
      "name": "Accounts & Finance",
      "path": "/dashboard/accounts",
      "icon": "📊",
      "sidebar_label": "ACCOUNTS & FINANCE",
      "permissions": [
        "CDO",
        "GM",
        "ADMIN",
        "ACC",
        "VISITOR"
      ],
      "ai_persona": "Sovereign Navigator",
      "ai_greeting_context": "You are Miracle — the Sovereign Navigator of Miracle OS. Guardian of wealth and financial health for the Sovereign Kernel.",
      "ai_knowledge": "ZONE 11 — ACCOUNTS & FINANCE (Sovereign Accounting Kernel — Full Enterprise Finance). This zone IS the financial backbone of Miracle OS. All money flows here automatically.\n\nTABS ON THIS PAGE:\n  TAB 0 — REVENUE VECTOR ANALYSIS: Shows a donut chart of Room Revenue vs F&B vs Other. Data comes from /accounting/ledger/live. Shows Total Net Revenue, Operational Load (COGS + Expenses), Net Margin, and Total Ledger Entries.\n  TAB 1 — ACCUSATIVE ITEM-WISE TRACE: Every single ledger entry — source, amount, timestamp, operator. This is the raw transaction log. Each row shows CREDIT (income) or DEBIT (expense), category, and value.\n  TAB 2 — BURDEN MATRIX: Shows Operational Expenses vs Payroll vs Commissions as visual progress bars. Useful for spotting which cost center is consuming the most.\n  TAB 3 — GL JOURNAL ENTRY: Post double-entry journal entries manually. Requires Account Code (debit & credit), Reference Number, and Description. Data comes from /accounting/coa/list (Chart of Accounts). Click POST TO SOVEREIGN LEDGER to save.\n  TAB 4 — CHART OF ACCOUNTS (COA): Lists all accounts: 1000=Cash, 1100=Advance Deposits, 1200=AR-Guests, 2100=Advance Deposit Liability, 4000=Room Revenue, 4100=F&B Revenue, 5000=Payroll Expense, 5200=Cost of Goods Sold, etc.\n  TAB 5 — AR AGING (Accounts Receivable): Outstanding guest payments by age (0-30 days, 31-60, 61-90, 90+ days). Data from /accounting/ar/aging. Shows guest name, folio ID, balance due, and days outstanding.\n  TAB 6 — AP MODULE (Accounts Payable): Outstanding vendor invoices. Shows vendor list and invoice aging. Data from /accounting/ap/invoices and /accounting/ap/vendors. Can ADD VENDOR and AUTHORIZE DISBURSEMENT.\n  TAB 7 — BANK RECONCILIATION: Match bank statement entries against ledger. Add bank entries, match them, and COMMIT RECEIPT.\n  TAB 8 — NIGHT AUDIT WIZARD: End-of-day 4-step process: (1) Blind Cash Count, (2) Inventory Water Count, (3) FO-HK Discrepancy Check, (4) Final Lock. Click RUN TRIAL BALANCE to verify ledger balance.\n\nDATA SOURCES: Every checkout (Z-08), every POS sale (Z-06), every payroll push (Z-09) auto-posts a double-entry here. The ledger is append-only (immutable). Revenue categories: ROOM_REVENUE, FB_REVENUE, OTHER_REVENUE. Expense categories: EXPENSE_PAYROLL, EXPENSE_COGS, EXPENSE_OPS.\n\nKEY METRICS FROM SQL:\n  Total Revenue: SELECT SUM(amount) FROM accounting_ledger WHERE type='CREDIT' AND category LIKE 'REVENUE%'\n  Net Profit: Revenue - Expenses - (Revenue*0.15 VAT)\n  AR Outstanding: SELECT SUM(balance - advance_paid) FROM guest_folios WHERE status='IN_HOUSE'\n\n[EXACT UI BUTTONS: RUN TRIAL BALANCE, POST TO SOVEREIGN LEDGER, ADD BANK ENTRY, COMMIT RECEIPT, AUTHORIZE DISBURSEMENT, ADD VENDOR TO DIRECTORY, AUTO-FIX, Simulate Discrepancy, PROCEED TO MASTER LOCK]"
    },
    {
      "id": "Z-19",
      "name": "Policy Engine",
      "path": "/dashboard/policy",
      "icon": "⚙️",
      "sidebar_label": "POLICY ENGINE",
      "permissions": [
